  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Because the collision is perfectly inelastic, hence the two blocks stick together. By conservation of linear momentum,<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mtext>V</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">mv</mtext></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>V</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br />By conservation of energy,<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">mgh</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mn>2</mn><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mtext><msup><mtext>V</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">h</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>g</mi></math>",
